00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
Five Nights at Freddy's 2 is a 2025 American supernatural horror film based on the video game series Five
Nights at Freddy's created by Scott Cawthon and the sequel to the 2023 film adaptation.

12
00:56:43,636 --> 00:56:49,636
The film was directed by Emma Tammi and written by Cawthon.

13
01:01:27,272 --> 01:01:33,272
Josh Hutcherson, Elizabeth Lail, Piper Rubio, and Matthew Lillard reprise their roles from the
previous film, with Mckenna Grace, Wayne Knight, and Skeet Ulrich joining the cast.

14
01:06:10,909 --> 01:06:16,909
Set a year and a half after the previous film, it follows Abby Schmidt (Rubio) as she gets manipulated by the
Marionette, an animatronic from the original Freddy Fazbear's Pizza who aims to plot revenge against parents.

15
01:10:54,545 --> 01:11:00,545
Cawthon stated in August 2018 that there could be a second Five Nights at Freddy's film, based on
the events of the series' second video game, if the first film were successful.

16
01:15:38,181 --> 01:15:44,181
Hutcherson revealed the development of a sequel in January 2024, with
Blumhouse Productions confirming it three months later.

17
01:20:21,818 --> 01:20:27,818
Principal photography began in November 2024 and concluded in
February 2025 in New Orleans and surrounding communities.

18
01:25:05,454 --> 01:25:11,454
Five Nights at Freddy's 2 premiered at the TCL Chinese Theater on December 2, 2025, and
was released in the United States by Universal Pictures on December 5.

19
01:29:49,090 --> 01:29:55,090
Similar to its predecessor, the film received negative reviews from critics and was a commercial
success, grossing $237.8 million worldwide against a budget between $36–51 million.

20
01:34:32,727 --> 01:34:38,727
The film explores themes of killer robot, pizzeria,
sequel, serial killer, security guard.

21
01:39:16,363 --> 01:39:22,363
The tone is intense and uplifting and dark.
